/* No Donuts — Localizable.strings (English, development language). ND-101.

   KEY CONVENTION: keys are the English source text itself, exactly as written in
   Swift (SwiftUI Text("…")/Button("…")/Section("…") literals are LocalizedStringKeys,
   and String(localized: "…") uses its literal as the key). So this file is an identity
   map, kept so every key is listed for translators and so en/fr key sets can be diffed.
   Consequences:
     - Editing English copy in Swift CHANGES THE KEY: update this file and every other
       <lang>.lproj/Localizable.strings with the same key (a stale key silently falls
       back to the English text).
     - Interpolations become format specifiers in the key: a String -> %@, an Int -> %lld.
       Translations with 2+ arguments use positional specifiers (%1$@, %2$@) so word
       order can change.
     - Keys that need plural forms (%lld min left, %lld seconds, ...) live ONLY in
       Localizable.stringsdict, never here.
   Not localized on purpose: the Copy Diagnostics report (support artifact, English),
   log messages, and strings produced by NoDonutsCore (protection-audit reasons,
   camera-unavailable reasons, lock-mechanism names).
   Tooling: CLT-only build, so no .xcstrings String Catalog (needs xcstringstool).
   Validate with `plutil -lint`. Resources/*.lproj are copied by scripts/make-app.sh. */

